              heading: 'Part 11',
              text: 'These barriers show why schools and communities must work together to make sports inclusive for everyone. The Meaning of “Paralympic” The word Paralympic comes from the Greek word para (meaning “beside” or “alongside”) and the word olympic. This illustrates that the Paralympic Games are held parallel to the Olympic Games, giving athletes with disabilities the same chance to compete at an international level. The Paralympic Games The Paralympic Games are the highest level of competition for elite athletes with physical disabilities. Just like Olympic athletes, Paralympians train hard, follow strict qualification rules, and compete with the goal of achieving their personal best — and a gold medal. The Paralympics give athletes with disabilities an environment of excellence, fairness, and pride. TRIVIA At present, the Paralympic Games include sports — summer sports and winter sports. These sports are adapted to allow athletes with different types of disabilities to compete at the highest level. Unit 4.indd 11-04-2026 03:41:31 Sports and Disability Opportunities for Paralympic Athletes Through the Paralympic Games, athletes with disabilities get the chance to: • Pursue their goals and ambitions in sport. • Dream of medals and international recognition. • Train rigorously with discipline and commitment. • Qualify by merit, meeting high international standards. • Showcase excellence, courage, and determination to the world. LET US REFLECT Which barrier do you think hinders participation the most? Discuss with your classmates and try to identify possible solutions. Activity Match the following.',
