              heading: 'Part 1',
              text: 'Yoga for Holistic Health and Personal Excellence U N I T Yoga is a continuous journey of awareness and self-development. By the end of Grade 8, we explored the values of Yama and Niyama, learned to move our body gently through Sūkṣhma-vyāyāma, understood the importance of practising Sūrya-namaskāra regularly, and became familiar with Āsanas that keep the body steady and comfortable. We also developed breath awareness through prāṇāyāma, learned to guide our senses wisely with Pratyāhāra, and discovered how to focus the mind through Dhāraṇā and Dhyāna. With this strong and balanced foundation, we are now ready to deepen our yogic journey and understand these practices with greater clarity. In Grade 9, we will build on everything we have learned so far, deepening our understanding and practice. The uniqueness of Unit lies in its simple and practical appr oach to the three main themes, Samagra Svāsthya (Yoga for Holistic Health), Yogamaya Jīvana (Lifestyle for Holistic Health) and Yoga for Personal Excellence . Samagra Svāsthya introduces the definition of health, meaning of holistic health, the states of ease and disease, as well as the various dimensions of health. Yogamaya Jīvana highlights different lifestyle factors such as āhāra (food), nidrā (sleep), brahmacharya (moderation), good company, behaviour, circadian rhythm, and habit formation. It offers simple tools to help students manage the challenges of adolescence. The chapter also shows how yoga improves focus, emotional balance, confidence, and menstrual health. Yoga for Personal Excellence guides students to choose the path of Śhreyas (long-term excellence) over Preyas (temporary pleasure). Through the inspiring stories of contemporary role models, students learn that true success is achieved by connecting hard work to a ‘higher goal’ beyond oneself.',
